config ETHOSU_ARM
        bool "ARM Ethos-U NPU driver (built-in)"
        depends on OF && HAS_IOMEM
        select DMA_SHARED_BUFFER
        help
          Say Y here to enable the ARM Ethos-U NPU driver as built-in.

          This driver provides a complete inference pipeline for ARM Ethos-U
          Neural Processing Units, including TensorFlow Lite model support,
          buffer management, and job scheduling.

          This is the full-featured ARM driver stack integrated as built-in
          kernel driver (no loadable modules required).

          If unsure, say Y for embedded platforms.

config ETHOSU_RPMSG
        bool "ARM Ethos-U NPU RPMSG interface"
        depends on ETHOSU_ARM && RPMSG
        help
          Say Y here to enable the RPMSG interface for subsystem configuration.

          This interface allows communication with a remote processor
          (e.g. Cortex-M) that manages the NPU in subsystem mode.

          Say N for direct drive configuration (recommended for embedded).

config ETHOSU_DIRECT
        bool "ARM Ethos-U NPU direct drive"
        depends on ETHOSU_ARM
        default y
        help
          Say Y here to enable direct drive configuration where the host
          CPU manages the NPU directly without a separate subsystem.

          This is the recommended configuration for embedded platforms
          as it has lower memory overhead and complexity.

          If unsure, say Y.
